<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">The model measured the total present value of
the Company&#8217;s proceeds at approximately $<ix:nonFraction contextRef="c0" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:ProceedsFromOtherDebt" scale="0" unitRef="usd" id="ixv-7353">7,838</ix:nonFraction> and the total present value of the Company&#8217;s liability at approximately $<ix:nonFraction contextRef="c2" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:OtherLiabilities" scale="0" unitRef="usd" id="ixv-7354">1,142,277</ix:nonFraction>,
resulting in a net liability of approximately $<ix:nonFraction contextRef="c2" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:FairValueNetAssetLiability" scale="0" unitRef="usd" id="ixv-7355">1,134,400</ix:nonFraction> as of March&#160;31, 2025. This resulted in a non-cash gain from the change in
fair value of derivatives of approximately $<ix:nonFraction contextRef="c0" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:FairValueOptionChangesInFairValueGainLoss1" scale="0" unitRef="usd" id="ixv-7356">5,269,700</ix:nonFraction> for the three months ended March 31, 2025.</p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&#160;</p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><b><i>Warrants &#8211; Series A and B</i></b></p>

